# Canonical identities, so `git shortlog` and `git log` count one person once.
#
# Both of us have committed under two addresses — a GitHub noreply and a
# personal one — which git treats as four contributors rather than two. The
# left-hand side of each line is the canonical identity; the right-hand side is
# the address to fold into it.
#
# What this does NOT do, since it came up: GitHub does not read .mailmap. Its
# contributors graph works from the email addresses connected to a GitHub
# account, so the way to make the personal addresses attribute correctly there
# is to add them under Settings → Emails on the account itself. And neither has
# any bearing on Actions billing, which is charged per licensed seat and by
# minutes used.
#
#   https://docs.github.com/en/account-and-profile/how-tos/email-preferences/adding-an-email-address-to-your-github-account

